that kind of enables it to, to sort of handle these things for you.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:16.010
So, the first thing that Rocket does a little differently is that it has no global state.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.920
If you use basically any other web framework,

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.780
there is usually something global.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.920
The application is global,

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.050
the request is global, there's some global state.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.940
In Rocket, that's just not the case.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.035
In Rocket, everything is sort of a function,

00:07:28.035 --> 00:07:30.010
and the function's parameters,

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.270
the function's declaration contains

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:35.855
all the information necessary to validate and process that request.

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:37.745
There is nothing outside of that function.

00:07:37.745 --> 00:07:39.140
If you see it in the function,

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:44.160
it's going to be used and if it's not in the function, it cannot be used.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:49.155
The second is that all of the requests

00:07:49.155 --> 00:07:54.165
that are processed by a Rocket application are guaranteed to have been validated.

00:07:54.165 --> 00:07:56.640
So, before any processing happens,

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:00.030
before your code actually executes on a request,

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.040
then Rocket has ensured that,

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.650
that request has been validated according to your own policies,

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.600
according to your sort of arbitrary policies.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.735
And this sort of is happening at the type level.

00:08:09.735 --> 00:08:11.460
So, as you see in the second, we have these types that

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.785
dictate sort of what things must be true about the request,

00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:15.780
and Rocket will ensure that those things in fact are

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.555
true before it passes you a value of that type.

00:08:18.555 --> 00:08:21.760
In fact, it can't pass you a value of that type unless those things are true.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.630
And finally, everything in Rocket is extensible.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.060
Rocket's core is really, really small.

