Okay. So, destroy is actually going to be

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.960
the method that's going to be sort of vulnerable here.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:07.245
So, what they've written is.

00:20:07.245 --> 00:20:11.685
If this destroy method gets called at any point by Rails don't authenticate the admin,

00:20:11.685 --> 00:20:13.210
but do authenticate the impersonator.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:16.595
[NOISE] It sounds okay I suppose.

00:20:16.595 --> 00:20:20.235
So, what sort of goes wrong sort of what this destroying method does is it you know,

00:20:20.235 --> 00:20:23.080
checks if there's an impersonator logged in,

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.940
and it sets the user to be able to be

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:27.085
