00:20:27.085 --> 00:20:31.295
and uh, you sort of redirect to wherever you need to go,

00:20:31.295 --> 00:20:34.540
you know, to the- the person you're impersonating's page.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.680
[NOISE] And the hope is that this destroy method doesn't

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:39.675
run unless the person is allowed to impersonate someone.

00:20:39.675 --> 00:20:42.050
Because if it can, well then anyone can be anyone they want.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:46.845
And the problem is that this authorized impersonator method is is wrong

00:20:46.845 --> 00:20:52.715
because if there is not an impersonator ID in the session, then if this case does run,

00:20:52.715 --> 00:20:55.255
and you don't do any authentication at all.

00:20:55.255 --> 00:20:57.715
And because it's Ruby, you sort of get this nil

00:20:57.715 --> 00:21:01.420
which I don't know, presumably evaluates to true or something,

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:05.730
uh, and then this destroy method just kind of runs which is just pretty bad.

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:07.980
So, clearly this would look nothing,

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:11.060
I mean we would just have like an impersonator type in Rocket and we

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:14.790
would sort of guard this destroy method by that type and none of this would happen.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.310
[NOISE] Okay.

